# Supabase deploy (Furniture 1000)

When you add or change **SQL migrations** (`supabase/migrations/`) or **edge functions** (`supabase/functions/`), deploy them yourself in the same session. Do not only tell the user to run commands manually.

## Project

| Item | Value |
|------|-------|
| Project ref | `riaubhtruisbwdlwjzur` |
| Project name | Furniture 1000 |
| CLI | `npx supabase` (devDependency `supabase@2.x`) |
| Auth | `SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN` (already in cloud env) |

Link once per session if needed:

```bash
npx supabase link --project-ref riaubhtruisbwdlwjzur --yes
```

## 1. Migrations

**Prefer targeted apply** for new migration files (remote history may not match local `supabase/migrations/`):

```bash
# Check table/object does not already exist
curl -s -X POST "https://api.supabase.com/v1/projects/riaubhtruisbwdlwjzur/database/query" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"query":"select to_regclass('\''public.<table>'\'') as exists;"}'

# Apply single migration
SQL=$(cat supabase/migrations/<file>.sql | python3 -c 'import json,sys; print(json.dumps(sys.stdin.read()))')
curl -s -X POST "https://api.supabase.com/v1/projects/riaubhtruisbwdlwjzur/database/migrations" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d "{\"name\":\"<migration_slug>\",\"query\":$SQL}"
```

- `migration_slug` = filename without date prefix (e.g. `20260714_create_platform_user_profiles.sql` → `create_platform_user_profiles`).
- After apply: verify columns/table exist, then `notify pgrst, 'reload schema';`.

**Avoid** `npx supabase db push` unless the user explicitly asks — local/remote migration history is out of sync and a full push can be risky.

## 2. Edge functions

Deploy new/changed functions automatically:

```bash
npx supabase functions deploy <function-folder-name> \
  --project-ref riaubhtruisbwdlwjzur \
  --no-verify-jwt
```

This repo also uses **prefixed slugs** for many functions. After CLI deploy, also deploy the prefixed alias (same as `scripts/deploy-edge-functions.ps1`):

```bash
# slug = supabase-functions-<function-folder-name>
curl -s -X POST "https://api.supabase.com/v1/projects/riaubhtruisbwdlwjzur/functions/deploy?slug=supabase-functions-<name>" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN" \
  -F "metadata=@/tmp/meta.json;type=application/json" \
  -F "file=@supabase/functions/<name>/index.ts"
```

`meta.json`: `{"name":"<name>","entrypoint_path":"index.ts","verify_jwt":false}`

Frontend invokes often try **prefixed slug first**, then bare name — deploy both when adding a new function.

Add new functions to `scripts/deploy-edge-functions.ps1` when created.

## 3. Verify

- Migration: query `information_schema.columns` or `to_regclass`.
- Function: unauthenticated POST should return `401 Unauthorized` (not 404).
- List functions: `GET https://api.supabase.com/v1/projects/riaubhtruisbwdlwjzur/functions`

## 4. Report to user

After deploy, briefly state:
- migration name + table verified, or
- function slug(s) + ACTIVE status.

## When to run

- User says「部署 migration / edge function / supabase」or similar.
- You created a migration or edge function as part of a feature — deploy before marking the task done.
- User confirms「已部署 supabase CLI」— treat as permission to run deploys yourself going forward.

## Skip when

- User explicitly says not to deploy to production.
- Only local/dev schema experiments with no remote intent.
- `SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN` is missing (report and stop).
